<title>AUSTRALIA: BHP remains silent on Foster's.</title>
<headline>BHP remains silent on Foster's.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) on Wednesday kept its silence on the future of its 37 percent stake in Foster's Brewing Group Ltd, after another shareholder said it was reviewing its relations with the brewer.</p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday, 14-percent shareholder Asahi Breweries Ltd told Reuters it wanted to put its relationship with the Australian brewer on a &quot;completely new&quot; footing.</p>
<p>Asked if BHP had an understanding with Asahi about any sell-down of their respective stakes, BHP declined comment.</p>
<p>&quot;I have not seen what Asahi has said and I have no comment,&quot; BHP spokesman Michael Spencer told Reuters.  </p>
<p>Foster's also declined to comment on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne Bureau 613-9286-1421</p>
</text>
